Q - 9) What is the difference between final, finally and finalize in Java?

		final
		------
		It is used to make a variable or a method or a class as unchangeable.
		The value of a variable can't be changed once it is initialized.
		A method can't be overridden class and a class declared as final can't be extended.
		finally
		-------
		finally is a block in Java which is used for exception handling
		finally block is always executed whether an exception is occurred or not and occurred exception is handled or not.
		It is used to close the resources like database connection, I/O resources
		finalize()
		----------
		It is used to perform some clean up operations on an object before it is removed from the memory.
		This method is called by garbage collector thread before an object is removed from the memory.
		This method is inherited to every class you create in Java.
Q-10) What is the difference between throw, throws and throwable in Java?
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
		throw
		-----
		throw is a keyword in Java which is used to throw an exception manually.
		Using throw keyword, you can throw an exception from any method or block. But, that exception must be of type java.lang.Throwable class or it's sub classes.
		throws
		------
		throws is also a keyword in java which is used in the method signature to indicate that this method may throw mentioned exceptions.
		The caller to such methods must handle the mentioned exceptions either using try-catch blocks or using throws keyword.
		Throwable
		--------
		Throwable is a super class for all types of errors and exceptions in Java.
		Only instances of this class or it's sub classes are thrown by the java virtual machine or by the throw statement.
